---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DesignTodo from './DesignTodo.astro';
import '../styles/steps.css';

const { locale = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const es = locale === 'es';
const A = '/projects/steps/';
const stages = es ? ['PREPARAR','EXFOLIAR','TRATAR','HIDRATAR','FINALIZAR'] : ['PREPARE','EXFOLIATE','TREAT','MOISTURIZE','FINISH'];
const products = es ? ['PREPARAR','TRATAR','ACONDICIONAR','FINALIZAR','CUIDADO EN CASA'] : ['PREP','TREAT','CONDITION','FINISH','AFTERCARE'];
const capabilities = ['Brand Strategy','Visual Identity','Packaging Design','Product Systems','Art Direction','Retail Communication','Service Design','Digital Extension'];
---

<BaseLayout locale={locale} title="Steps" description="Steps — a brand, product and care experience system.">
<article class="st">
	<header class="st-hero st-wrap">
		<a class="st-back" href={`${es ? '/es/' : '/'}#projects`}>← {es ? 'Todos los proyectos' : 'All projects'}</a>
		<div class="st-meta"><span>STEPS / PROFESSIONAL CARE · BEAUTY · PACKAGING</span><span>ORIGINAL WORK + CONTEMPORARY EXTENSIONS</span></div>
		<h1>{es ? 'Diseñando un ritual del tratamiento al anaquel.' : 'Designing a ritual from treatment room to shelf.'}</h1>
		<p>{es ? 'Steps nació como una marca de pedicure especializado donde el cuidado profesional y la experiencia sensorial debían sentirse parte del mismo sistema. La identidad se extendió a packaging, producto y comunicación mediante materiales táctiles, tipografía contenida y un pattern reconocible. Este caso revisita el trabajo original y explora cómo esa base puede crecer hoy hacia una experiencia más amplia.' : 'Steps was developed as a specialized pedicure brand where professional care and sensory experience needed to feel part of the same system. The identity extended across packaging, product applications and brand communication, combining tactile materials, restrained typography and a recognizable graphic pattern. This case study revisits that original work and explores how the same foundation could expand today into a broader service and product experience.'}</p>
	</header>
	<section class="st-hero-art st-wide">
		<img src={`${A}steps1.webp`} alt="Steps specialized pedicures reception and product experience" fetchpriority="high" />
	</section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>01</b><div><small>01 / CONTEXT</small><h2>{es ? 'El cuidado profesional empieza antes del tratamiento.' : 'Professional care needs to feel considered before the treatment begins.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'Un servicio especializado se experimenta antes de aplicar cualquier producto. El nombre, el espacio, el packaging, los materiales, el lenguaje y los objetos usados durante el servicio construyen la percepción de cuidado. La oportunidad fue crear un sistema donde calidad profesional y calma sensorial pudieran coexistir.' : 'A specialized care service is experienced before any product is applied. The customer encounters the name, the space, the packaging, the materials, the language and the objects used during the service. Each moment contributes to the perception of care. The opportunity was to create a visual system where professional quality and sensory calm could coexist.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-sequence st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí treatment sequence" />{(es ? ['DESCUBRIR','LLEGAR','TRATAMIENTO','PRODUCTO','CUIDADO POSTERIOR'] : ['DISCOVER','ARRIVE','TREATMENT','PRODUCT','AFTERCARE']).map((x,i)=><div><span>0{i+1}</span><strong>{x}</strong><i>↓</i></div>)}</section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>02</b><div><small>02 / BRAND STRATEGY</small><h2>{es ? 'El cuidado sucede en pasos.' : 'Care happens in steps.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'El nombre ofrecía una idea organizadora sencilla. Un pedicure no es una sola acción: preparación, tratamiento, atención, acabado y cuidado posterior. La identidad usa esa progresión como principio estructural, no como motivo literal. Repetición, ritmo y continuidad forman el lenguaje de marca.' : 'The name offered a simple organizing idea. A pedicure is not one action. It is a sequence: preparation, treatment, attention, finish and aftercare. The identity uses that sense of progression as a structural principle rather than as a literal visual motif. Repetition, rhythm and continuity become part of the brand language.'}<em>ORIGINAL PROFESSIONAL WORK</em></p></div></section>
	<section class="st-brand st-wide"><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_71.webp`} alt="Original Steps logo and branded applications" /><div class="st-wordmark">Steps<small>SPECIALIZED PEDICURES</small></div><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí identidad original Steps" /></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>03</b><div><small>03 / VISUAL SYSTEM</small><h2>{es ? 'Una identidad táctil construida con repetición.' : 'A tactile identity built from repetition.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'Un pattern ondulado recurrente aporta textura sin depender de fotografía. La repetición sugiere ritmo, tacto y continuidad, y funciona en cajas, etiquetas, papelería y aplicaciones mayores sin competir con la identidad.' : 'A recurring wave pattern gives the system texture without relying on photography. Its repetition suggests rhythm, touch and continuity while providing a flexible surface that can move between packaging, tags, stationery and larger applications. The pattern works as a recognizable layer beneath the identity rather than competing with it.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-pattern-study st-wide"><div></div><div></div><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_8841.webp`} alt="Original Steps wave pattern" /><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: mostrar aquí pattern original a gran escala" /></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>04</b><div><small>04 / MATERIAL LANGUAGE</small><h2>{es ? 'Cálido, táctil, contenido.' : 'Warm, tactile, restrained.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'El sistema histórico trabaja con marrones cálidos, neutros naturales y acentos violetas controlados: colores que viven con naturalidad en papel, vidrio ámbar, tela y packaging.' : 'The historical system uses warm browns, natural neutrals and controlled violet accents. Those colors work particularly well across paper, amber glass, fabric and product packaging.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-materials st-wide">{[['#3b2119','DARK BROWN'],['#8a4e2f','AMBER GLASS'],['#d8c9ba','CREAM PAPER'],['#7541ae','VIOLET ACCENT'],['#f4efe8','WHITE TYPE']].map(([c,n])=><div style={`--swatch:${c}`}><span>{n}</span></div>)}</section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>05</b><div><small>05 / PACKAGING</small><h2>{es ? 'El producto debe seguir pareciendo Steps cuando el logo se hace pequeño.' : 'The product should still look like Steps when the logo gets smaller.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'El packaging es una de las expresiones más fuertes de la identidad. Tipografía, color, pattern y jerarquía trabajan juntos para crear parentesco sin convertir cada envase en el mismo objeto.' : 'Packaging is one of the strongest expressions of the identity. At small scale, typography, color, pattern and hierarchy work together so information remains recognizable without turning every container into the same object.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-packaging st-wide"><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_prev.webp`} alt="Original Steps Chocolate Lotion bottle and box" /><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_8271.webp`} alt="Original Steps packaging and product details" /><img src={`${A}download.webp`} alt="Original Steps amber dropper bottle" /><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí packaging original" /></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>06</b><div><small>06 / PRODUCT SYSTEM</small><em>CONTEMPORARY SYSTEM EXTRACTION</em><h2>{es ? 'Una familia. Distintas funciones.' : 'One family. Different functions.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'La exploración contemporánea extrae una lógica simple de la marca original para ordenar tratamientos por nombre, función, formato, tamaño y secuencia opcional. Esta taxonomía es conceptual; no se presenta como parte del sistema histórico.' : 'The contemporary exploration extracts a simple logic from the original brand so different treatments can be organized through product name, function, format, size and optional sequence. This is a conceptual contemporary taxonomy, not a claim about the historical system.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-products st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí conceptual product family" />{products.map((x,i)=><article><span>0{i+1}</span><div class={`bottle b${i}`}></div><h3>{x}</h3><small>{[100,150,120,75,50][i]} ML · SAMPLE</small></article>)}</section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>07</b><div><small>07 / PACKAGING INFORMATION</small><h2>{es ? 'El lujo también necesita legibilidad.' : 'Luxury still needs legibility.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'La etiqueta separa marca expresiva e información práctica: producto, función, volumen, uso e ingredientes permanecen visibles.' : 'The label separates expressive branding from practical information: product, function, volume, usage and ingredients remain visible.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-label st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí label hierarchy" /><div><b>Steps</b><span>03 / CONDITION</span><h3>CHOCOLATE LOTION</h3><small>150 ML · SAMPLE PRODUCT COPY</small></div><div><span>FUNCTION</span><p>Conditioning lotion for use during the Restore treatment.</p><span>USAGE</span><p>Apply a small amount and massage until absorbed.</p><span>INGREDIENTS</span><p>Sample product copy — final formulation required.</p></div></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>08</b><div><small>08 / SERVICE SYSTEM</small><em>CONTEMPORARY EXTENSION</em><h2>{es ? 'Convertir la línea de producto en un ritual visible.' : 'Turn the product line into a visible ritual.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'La misma secuencia puede estructurar el servicio. Cada etapa adquiere un papel y una señal visual sin volver rígido el tratamiento: hace que el cuidado se sienta deliberado.' : 'The same sequence used to organize products can structure the service itself. Each stage has a clear role and visual cue without turning treatment into a rigid process. It makes care feel deliberate.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-treatment st-wide">{stages.map((x,i)=><article><span>0{i+1}</span><div class={`mini-product m${i}`}></div><h3>{x}</h3><p>{es ? ['Limpiar y preparar','Renovar suavemente','Aplicar cuidado específico','Restaurar humedad','Proteger y concluir'][i] : ['Clean and prepare','Renew gently','Apply focused care','Restore moisture','Protect and complete'][i]}</p></article>)}</section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>09</b><div><small>09 / SERVICE COMMUNICATION</small><em>CONTEMPORARY EXTENSION</em><h2>{es ? 'Los servicios deben entenderse antes de reservar.' : 'Services should be easy to understand before they are booked.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'Un menú de tratamiento ofrece información suficiente para elegir con confianza sin abrumar.' : 'A treatment menu needs enough information to support a confident choice without overwhelming the customer.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-menu st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí treatment menu" /><header><b>STEPS</b><span>SIGNATURE CARE</span></header>{[['ESSENTIAL','30 MIN','01 · 02 · 05'],['RESTORE','45 MIN','01 · 02 · 03 · 04'],['COMPLETE','60 MIN','01 · 02 · 03 · 04 · 05']].map(x=><article><h3>{x[0]}</h3><b>{x[1]}</b><p>{x[2]}</p><small>{es ? 'Precio de muestra opcional' : 'Optional sample pricing'}</small></article>)}</section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>10</b><div><small>10 / IN-SERVICE COMMUNICATION</small><em>CONTEMPORARY EXTENSION</em><h2>{es ? 'Los pequeños detalles vuelven tangible el sistema.' : 'Small details make the system tangible.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'Una tarjeta identifica el servicio, productos usados, cuidado recomendado y un siguiente paso.' : 'A treatment card identifies the service performed, products used, recommended aftercare and a simple next step.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-cards st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí treatment / aftercare card" /><div><small>STEPS</small><h3>YOUR TREATMENT</h3><b>RESTORE / 45 MIN</b></div><div><span>PRODUCTS USED</span><p>02 / TREAT<br/>03 / CONDITION</p><span>AFTERCARE</span><p>Use 05 / AFTERCARE at home.</p></div></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>11</b><div><small>11 / AFTERCARE</small><em>CONTEMPORARY EXTENSION</em><h2>{es ? 'La experiencia continúa después de la cita.' : 'The experience can continue after the appointment.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'Una tarjeta o mensaje breve conecta el resultado del tratamiento con la rutina y el producto adecuado.' : 'A small card or digital message connects the treatment result to the routine and the right product.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-aftercare st-wide"><div><b>AFTER YOUR TREATMENT</b><span>TODAY</span><p>Keep the area clean and comfortable.</p><span>NEXT 48 HOURS</span><p>Follow the recommendation from your specialist.</p><span>AT HOME</span><p>Use 05 / AFTERCARE as directed.</p></div><div class="phone"><small>STEPS</small><p>Your aftercare guide is ready.</p><button>VIEW ROUTINE</button></div></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>12</b><div><small>12 / RETAIL</small><em>CONCEPTUAL EXTENSION</em><h2>{es ? 'Una familia de producto necesita vivir junta.' : 'A product family needs a way to live together.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'El display organiza producto por etapa, función, tamaño y ritual sin imaginar una tienda completa.' : 'The display organizes product through stage, function, size and ritual without inventing a complete store.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-retail st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí retail display" /><header>STEPS <span>CARE / IN SEQUENCE</span></header><div>{['01 PREP','02 TREAT','03 CONDITION','04 FINISH','05 AFTERCARE'].map((x,i)=><article><div class={`mini-product m${i}`}></div><b>{x}</b></article>)}</div></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>13</b><div><small>13 / SPATIAL BRAND</small><em>CONCEPTUAL EXTENSION</em><h2>{es ? 'Una identidad silenciosa a escala arquitectónica.' : 'A quiet identity at architectural scale.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'Wordmark, pattern, material y orientación llevan la marca al espacio sin convertirlo en showroom.' : 'Wordmark, pattern, material and wayfinding take the brand into space without turning it into a branded showroom.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-space st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí spatial signage" /><div class="wall"><b>Steps</b><span>TREATMENT 02 →</span></div><div class="glass">CARE<br/>IN<br/>SEQUENCE</div></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>14</b><div><small>14 / DIGITAL SERVICE</small><em>CONCEPTUAL EXTENSION</em><h2>{es ? 'De elegir tratamiento a reservar una cita.' : 'From treatment choice to appointment.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'Una experiencia ligera lleva la misma estructura al entorno digital: servicio, duración, fecha, hora y contacto.' : 'A lightweight booking experience carries the same service structure into digital: service, duration, date, time and contact.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-digital st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí booking interface" /><div class="booking"><small>SELECT TREATMENT</small><h3>RESTORE <span>45 MIN</span></h3><label>DATE <i>18 / 09 / 2026</i></label><label>TIME <i>11:30</i></label><label>CONTACT DETAILS <i>YOUR DETAILS</i></label><button>BOOK APPOINTMENT</button></div></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>15</b><div><small>15 / DIGITAL PRODUCT</small><em>CONCEPTUAL EXTENSION</em><h2>{es ? 'Explicar el producto sin perder el tono sensorial.' : 'Explain the product without losing the sensory tone.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'La página comunica qué es, dónde entra en la rutina, cómo se usa, formato, tamaño y productos relacionados.' : 'The product page explains what the product is, where it fits in the routine, how it is used, format, size and related products.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-product-page st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí product detail interface" /><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_prev.webp`} alt="Original Steps Chocolate Lotion" /><div><small>03 / CONDITION</small><h3>CHOCOLATE<br/>LOTION</h3><b>150 ML</b><p>Sample product copy. Used in the Restore treatment.</p><button>ADD TO BAG</button></div></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>16</b><div><small>16 / IMAGE DIRECTION</small><h2>{es ? 'Material antes que atmósfera.' : 'Material before mood.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'La dirección conserva vidrio ámbar, papel marrón, superficies neutras, violeta controlado y detalle táctil. Evita piedras de spa, toallas blancas, bambú y clichés zen.' : 'Photography should make texture, product and touch visible: amber glass, brown paper, neutral surfaces, controlled violet and close tactile detail. Avoid spa stones, white towels, bamboo and universal wellness clichés.'}</p></div></section>
	<section class="st-photo-grid st-wide"><img src={`${A}download.webp`} alt="Amber glass and violet material detail"/><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_58.webp`} alt="Steps product family material study"/><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: crear moodboard con assets reales primero" /></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>17</b><div><small>17 / BRAND APPLICATION</small><h2>{es ? 'La identidad en objetos cotidianos.' : 'The identity in everyday objects.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'El lenguaje original se extiende naturalmente a comunicación de pequeño formato mediante pattern, tipografía y material.' : 'The original visual language extends naturally into small-format communication where pattern, type and material carry most of the identity.'}<em>ORIGINAL PROFESSIONAL WORK</em></p></div></section>
	<section class="st-stationery st-wide"><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_2.webp`} alt="Original Steps stationery, card, tag and announcement"/><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_71.webp`} alt="Original Steps physical brand communication"/><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí stationery original" /></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>18</b><div><small>18 / ORIGINAL WORK</small><h2>{es ? 'El sistema como fue desarrollado originalmente.' : 'The system as originally developed.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'La identidad, packaging y aplicaciones pertenecen al trabajo profesional original desarrollado para Steps. Las extensiones de servicio, retail y digital mostradas antes son exploraciones posteriores construidas desde esa base.' : 'The identity, packaging and applications shown here belong to the original professional work developed for Steps. The contemporary service, retail and digital extensions presented elsewhere are later explorations built from that foundation.'}<em>ORIGINAL PROFESSIONAL WORK</em></p></div></section>
	<section class="st-archive st-wide">{['Branding-for-Beauty-industry_58.webp','Branding-for-Beauty-industry_8271.webp','Branding-for-Beauty-industry_2.webp','Branding-for-Beauty-industry_71.webp','download.webp'].map((x,i)=><img src={`${A}${x}`} alt={`Steps original professional work ${i+1}`} loading="lazy"/>)}<DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí original professional archive" /></section>

	<section class="st-copy st-wrap"><b>19</b><div><small>19 / CONTEMPORARY EXTENSION</small><h2>{es ? 'De identidad a sistema completo de cuidado.' : 'From identity to complete care system.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'La obra original relacionó producto, packaging y lenguaje táctil. La revisión vuelve explícita esa lógica: los productos forman una familia, la familia una secuencia y la secuencia se extiende a tratamiento, aftercare, retail y booking.' : 'The original project established a strong relationship between product, packaging and tactile brand language. Revisiting Steps makes that system explicit: products become a family, the family becomes a sequence, and the sequence extends into treatment, aftercare, retail and booking.'}<em>2026 CONCEPTUAL EXTENSION</em></p></div></section>
	<section class="st-ecosystem st-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí final Steps care ecosystem" /><div><b>PRODUCT</b><b>PACKAGING</b><b>TREATMENT</b><b>AFTERCARE</b><b>BOOKING</b><b>RETAIL</b></div><img src={`${A}Branding-for-Beauty-industry_58.webp`} alt="Steps original product family anchoring the care ecosystem"/></section>

	<section class="st-reflection st-wrap"><b>20</b><div><small>20 / REFLECTION</small><h2>{es ? 'Una marca gana valor cuando cada detalle sabe dónde pertenece.' : 'A brand becomes more valuable when every detail knows where it belongs.'}</h2><p>{es ? 'El logotipo crea reconocimiento. El pattern crea textura. El packaging crea lenguaje físico. La arquitectura de producto crea orden. La comunicación de servicio crea continuidad. Juntos convierten piezas aisladas en experiencia.' : 'The logotype creates recognition. Pattern creates texture. Packaging creates a physical language. Product architecture creates order. Service communication creates continuity. Together, those elements turn individual pieces into an experience.'}</p><div>{capabilities.map(x=><span>{x}</span>)}</div><em>Original professional identity and packaging work + selected contemporary conceptual extensions.</em></div></section>
	<footer class="st-final st-wide"><span>STEPS / CARE AS A SEQUENCE</span><h2>CARE<br/><i>01—05</i></h2><p>BRAND + PRODUCT + SERVICE</p></footer>
</article>
</BaseLayout>
